/-!
# The exact pairing radical in the remaining cubic branch

Let R = U_I intersect C_G(O₂(I)). If the selected common commutator
is centralized by O₂(I), its order-two actor fixes U_I/R. Normality
of this action kernel puts the whole selected dihedral factor in it.
Minimality then puts the original five-core in the same kernel, and
lifting through O₂(I) bounds the full two-perfect lift's movement by R.

Since I is generated by that lift and L₁T, U_I = V R. Natural seed
geometry and the actual point-core movement give V intersect R = V₁.
Consequently U_I/R and its literal dual O₂(I)/C_{O₂(I)}(U_I) have
order four. The full radical and all original quotient maps are retained.
These restrictions do not by themselves exclude the cubic branch.
The original-witness application is in LargePrimeCubicRadicalSource.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, 14.5.21(1), 14.7.6, printed pp.1019 and
1044–1045, refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/

public noncomputable section
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter14.Section07.LocalStructure.CriticalFusion.SourceConstruction.LocalReduction
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Representation Representation.BinaryOffender
open Chapter12.Section08 CriticalFusion.Source ChapterD
